": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52323, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018Qnhs4Md9Z1AE5286SCghP", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 53509, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QWRot3iyZKAHibKBJ5UNB6", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53809, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QWRot3iyZKAHibKBJ5UNB6", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53809, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QWRot3iyZKAHibKBJ5UNB6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 58670, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. A SEV2 incident is open and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Starting state:** all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were on v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with about an 18% error rate.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy, so I didn't use it.\n- **What happened:** the first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. I checked the regions, found us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two still on v2.3.1, and ran it again. The second attempt finished.\n- **Now:** all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list and found it had been created: INC-0001, SEV2, checkout-api, status open. I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- The incident summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the orchestrator error partway through, and the current healthy state. It lists two follow-ups: find out what broke in v2.3.1, and find out what caused the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LNCeXz9t2MzskxnnWkg5jq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01G2br6jMB8uVrk7ceNm6n2z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TvhztNfVAad4iGiaRCUAuG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Dr9a344b7cFuYaN5eL9dXT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EPSu8J7btQLFCDZ5cydNVB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TzPPM5wbuZBGZztesBcuFt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PyNJHJNWvh1bv8woN8rfWe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018Qnhs4Md9Z1AE5286SCghP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A second attempt completed the rollout. All regions are now on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 regression and orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QWRot3iyZKAHibKBJ5UNB6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. A SEV2 incident is open and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Starting state:** all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were on v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with about an 18% error rate.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The release candidate for v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy, so I didn't use it.\n- **What happened:** the first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. I checked the regions, found us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two still on v2.3.1, and ran it again. The second attempt finished.\n- **Now:** all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list and found it had been created: INC-0001, SEV2, checkout-api, status open. I didn't resend it, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- The incident summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the orchestrator error partway through, and the current healthy state. It lists two follow-ups: find out what broke in v2.3.1, and find out what caused the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}